---
import Lab from '../layouts/Lab.astro';
import TubeBank from '../components/TubeBank.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Shot from '../components/Shot.astro';
import { u, repo } from '../lib/url';

const install = u('/docs/getting-started/install-from-source/');
---
<Lab
  title="Lucia · The homelab that takes the 2 a.m. shift"
  description="Lucia runs your homelab from an NVIDIA DGX Spark: PXE-installed Debian servers, AdGuard on every node, Docker apps, local AI, and scheduled assistant jobs that triage dead containers before you notice."
>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="hero-title" class="display">Lucia takes the <span class="lit-word">2&nbsp;a.m.</span> shift.</h1>
      <p class="lede prose-m">
        An on-call engineer and a homelab easy button in one box. Lucia onboards Debian servers, keeps DNS, apps and
        updates in line, and runs scheduled jobs that triage dead containers before you notice. It asks before anything
        destructive. You keep root. You just stop needing it.
      </p>
      <div class="ctas">
        <Button kind="lit" href={install}>Install from source</Button>
        <Button href={repo} external>Star on GitHub</Button>
        <Button kind="soon">Desktop bootstrap</Button>
      </div>
      <p class="fine">MIT licensed. Runs on your hardware, on your network, under your accounts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="instrument" role="group" aria-label="Shift clock">
      <div class="inst-top">
        <span class="engr">Shift clock</span>
        <span class="engr on-duty"><span class="lamp-on" aria-hidden="true"></span>Lucia on duty</span>
      </div>
      <TubeBank value="02:00" size="xl" label="The clock reads 02:00, the hour Lucia covers" class="clock" />
      <div class="inst-scale" aria-hidden="true"><span class="engr">Hours</span><span class="engr">Minutes</span></div>
      <dl class="readout">
        <div><dt class="engr">Mode</dt><dd>Asks first</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="engr">Owner</dt><dd>Asleep</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="engr">Status</dt><dd>Handling it</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="rack" class="rack-sec" aria-labelledby="rack-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2 id="rack-title" class="h2">Everything you used to babysit.</h2>
        <p class="prose-m">
          Each channel is a chore Lucia now watches, fixes or asks you about. Numbers in the tubes come from the source
          code or a working lab, not a slide deck.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rack">
        <article class="ch ch-feature" aria-labelledby="ch-jobs">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <TubeBank value="07:00" size="lg" label="A job scheduled for 7:00 every day" />
            <p class="plate engr">Daily, 7:00</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-jobs" class="h3">Assistant jobs</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              Saved prompts on a cron schedule. Every run opens its own chat thread, uses only the actions you approved
              for that job, and sends a push notification to the devices you picked when it needs you.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/assistant-and-jobs/')}>How jobs work</a>
          </div>
          <Shot class="ch-shot" name="jobs" route="#/ai/jobs" alt="Lucia's Assistant jobs page: a job named Fix stopped containers, scheduled every day at 7:00, with its last run finished." />
        </article>

        <article class="ch" aria-labelledby="ch-nodes">
          <div class="ch-read ch-read-pair">
            <div><TubeBank value="30" size="md" label="30 seconds between server readings" /><p class="plate engr">Seconds per reading</p></div>
            <div><TubeBank value="13" size="md" label="Debian 13" /><p class="plate engr">Debian, PXE'd</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-nodes" class="h3">Servers without a monitor</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              Network-boot a box, approve the disk, and Lucia installs Debian 13 and enrolls it. From then on it reports
              CPU, memory, GPU and temperatures every 30 seconds.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/nodes/')}>Nodes and onboarding</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ch" aria-labelledby="ch-dns">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <ul class="lamps" aria-label="Example lab: two AdGuard instances">
              <li><span class="lamp-on" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>lucialab01</span><span class="engr">Primary · .230</span></li>
              <li><span class="lamp-on" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>lucialab02</span><span class="engr">Replica · .231</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="plate engr">Example lab</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-dns" class="h3">DNS that survives a reboot</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              AdGuard runs on every node, each on its own virtual IP. Change a filter on the primary and the replicas
              follow. Reboot a server and the house still resolves.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/adguard-ha/')}>AdGuard high availability</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ch ch-feature ch-flip" aria-labelledby="ch-ai">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <TubeBank value="200" size="lg" label="200 thousand tokens of context" />
            <p class="plate engr">Thousand tokens · TensorFold, example lab</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-ai" class="h3">Local AI on the Spark</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              One language model and one embedding model, served on the Spark's GB10 and reachable from your apps through
              Lucia's OpenAI-compatible API. Memory is budgeted so the rest of the system keeps breathing.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/local-ai/')}>Local AI</a>
          </div>
          <Shot class="ch-shot" name="playground" route="#/ai" alt="Lucia's Playground page with the hosted model Qwen3.8-Flash-Next ready, served context 200,000 tokens, backend TensorFold." />
        </article>

        <article class="ch" aria-labelledby="ch-domains">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <TubeBank value="443" size="md" label="HTTPS on port 443" />
            <p class="plate engr">Port, with a real certificate</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-domains" class="h3">Names and certificates</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              Connect a Cloudflare zone and every app gets a name under your domain and a Let's Encrypt certificate, with
              local DNS answered by AdGuard. Skip it and Lucia serves everything from its own private CA. Public access is
              off until you turn it on.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/networking-and-dns/')}>Networking and DNS</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ch" aria-labelledby="ch-id">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <svg class="keyswitch" viewBox="0 0 120 64" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="22" fill="#121316" stroke="#3a3d42" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="13" fill="#1c1e22" stroke="#5a6068" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <rect x="30" y="20" width="4" height="24" rx="1.5" fill="#a6acb4" transform="rotate(35 32 32)" />
              <circle cx="78" cy="22" r="3.5" fill="#ff8a00" />
              <circle cx="78" cy="42" r="3.5" fill="#3a3d42" />
              <path d="M88 22h22M88 42h22" stroke="#3a3d42" stroke-width="1.5" />
            </svg>
            <p class="plate engr">One account</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-id" class="h3">One sign-in for the lab</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              Authentik runs the front door. One account covers Lucia, the apps a person's groups can open, and, for
              owners, the servers themselves.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/identity/')}>Identity</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ch" aria-labelledby="ch-obs">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <TubeBank value="10" size="md" label="10 seconds between Spark samples" />
            <p class="plate engr">Seconds per Spark sample</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-obs" class="h3">Watching the watcher</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              Traces, metrics and logs from Lucia and your nodes land in Grafana, along with the inference server's
              Prometheus metrics. The Spark's own health is sampled every 10 seconds.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/observability/')}>Observability</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ch" aria-labelledby="ch-upd">
          <div class="ch-read">
            <ul class="lamps" aria-label="Update flow">
              <li><span class="lamp-step" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Check</span></li>
              <li><span class="lamp-step" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Install all</span></li>
              <li><span class="lamp-step" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Restart what changed</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="ch-copy">
            <h3 id="ch-upd" class="h3">Patch Tuesday, any day</h3>
            <p class="prose-m">
              Lucia lists the Spark's pending packages and security fixes, installs them in one pass or on a schedule, and
              restarts only the services still holding old files.
            </p>
            <a class="more" href={u('/docs/architecture/spark-updates/')}>Spark updates</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="job-run" class="run-sec wrap" aria-labelledby="run-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="run-title" class="h2">A job run, start to finish.</h2>
      <p class="prose-m">This is a real job from the lab that wrote this page. It runs at seven every morning.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="run">
      <figure class="job-card">
        <figcaption class="job-head">
          <span class="h3">Fix stopped containers</span>
          <span class="engr">Daily, 7:00</span>
        </figcaption>
        <p class="engr">Saved prompt</p>
        <blockquote>
          Scan all apps for failed containers that are offline that aren't supposed to be in the "Stopped" state. Pull
          the logs. Triage the issue, and resolve it as long as it does not require modification to the application. If
          it requires modifications, notify the user.
        </blockquote>
        <p class="engr">Allowed without asking</p>
        <ul class="perm">
          <li class="on"><span class="sw" aria-hidden="true"></span>Start, stop, restart and update apps</li>
          <li><span class="sw" aria-hidden="true"></span>Create and change custom apps</li>
          <li><span class="sw" aria-hidden="true"></span>Move apps between servers</li>
        </ul>
      </figure>

      <ol class="trace">
        <li>
          <span class="node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Detect</h3>
          <p>Checks every app for containers that are down but were never meant to be stopped.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Pull logs</h3>
          <p>Reads the failing container's logs on whichever server runs it.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Triage</h3>
          <p>Works out whether a restart will do, or whether the app itself needs changing.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Fix, if allowed</h3>
          <p>Restarts or updates the app, because this job was allowed to. Anything outside that list waits for you.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="last">
          <span class="node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Notify</h3>
          <p>Writes up what happened in the run's chat thread and pings your phone if you need to look.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="keys-sec" aria-labelledby="keys-title">
    <div class="wrap keys">
      <div class="keys-copy">
        <h2 id="keys-title" class="h2">The owner holds the keys.</h2>
        <p class="prose-m">
          Lucia is helpful the way a good junior engineer is helpful: it does the reading, shows its work, and asks
          before it touches anything that matters.
        </p>
        <dl class="modes">
          <div><dt class="engr">Plan</dt><dd>Changes nothing at all. It reads, reasons and tells you what it would do.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="engr">Execute</dt><dd>Makes the changes you have allowed. Everything else waits for your approval in the chat.</dd></div>
          <div><dt class="engr">Jobs</dt><dd>Act unasked only inside the permissions saved on that one job.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="prose-m always">
          In a chat it <strong>always asks first</strong> before deleting an app, restoring a backup, putting an app on
          the internet, updating or restarting a server, or running a command on one.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Shot name="assistant-settings" route="#/settings/assistant" alt="Lucia's Assistant settings: a list of changes it may make without asking, all unchecked by default." />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="assumptions" class="assume-sec wrap" aria-labelledby="assume-title">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 id="assume-title" class="h2">What Lucia assumes about your lab.</h2>
      <p class="prose-m">Opinionated on purpose. If your lab looks like this, setup is short. If it doesn't, read this first.</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="spec-plate">
      <div><dt class="engr">Controller</dt><dd>An NVIDIA DGX Spark on DGX OS, past NVIDIA's first-run setup. Lucia, Authentik and Local AI live here.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="engr">Gateway</dt><dd>UniFi Network. It stays your DHCP server; Lucia never brings its own.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="engr">Servers</dt><dd>Network-bootable machines that Debian 13 installs on. Lucia owns them after enrollment.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="engr">Domain</dt><dd>Optional. A Cloudflare zone and a scoped API token for public certificates; without one, a private CA.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="engr">Apps</dt><dd>Docker Compose. Each app is one Compose file placed on one server.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="engr">You</dt><dd>Comfortable with SSH, and happy to let something else hold the pager.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <a class="more" href={u('/docs/getting-started/requirements/')}>Full requirements</a>
  </section>

  <section class="notyet-sec wrap" aria-labelledby="notyet-title">
    <div class="notyet">
      <div>
        <h2 id="notyet-title" class="h2">Not yet.</h2>
        <p class="prose-m">Some tubes are still dark. We would rather say so than let you find out at 2 a.m.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="dark-list">
        <li>
          <div class="dark-read"><TubeBank value="08" size="sm" dim label="8 GiB held back" /><p class="plate engr">Coming soon</p></div>
          <div><h3 class="h3">Voice</h3><p class="prose-m">Wake word, speech and voice print sign-in are planned. Local AI already keeps 8 GiB free for them.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="dark-read"><TubeBank value="000" size="sm" blank label="No release yet" /><p class="plate engr">Coming soon</p></div>
          <div><h3 class="h3">Releases</h3><p class="prose-m">There is no packaged release. You build from source, and the docs walk you through it.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="dark-read"><TubeBank value="00" size="sm" blank label="No signed desktop download yet" /><p class="plate engr">Coming soon</p></div>
          <div><h3 class="h3">Desktop download</h3><p class="prose-m">The one-window setup app works today if you build it yourself. There's no signed download yet, so SmartScreen and Gatekeeper will grumble.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <a class="more" href={u('/docs/reference/limitations/')}>Every known limitation</a>
  </section>

  <section class="close-sec" aria-labelledby="close-title">
    <div class="wrap close">
      <h2 id="close-title" class="display">Go back to bed.</h2>
      <p class="prose-m">Lucia has the pager.</p>
      <div class="ctas">
        <Button kind="lit" href={install}>Install from source</Button>
        <Button href={repo} external>Star on GitHub</Button>
        <Button kind="soon">Desktop bootstrap</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <footer class="wrap foot">
      <span class="engr">Lucia</span>
      <a href={u('/docs/')}>Docs</a>
      <a href={repo} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">MIT License</a>
      <span class="foot-note">Screenshots are from a working lab, unretouched.</span>
    </footer>
  </section>
</Lab>

<style>
  /* Hero */
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr; gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: center; padding-block: clamp(40px, 7vw, 88px) clamp(48px, 7vw, 96px); }
  .lede { margin-top: 26px; font-size: 1.125rem; max-width: 50ch; }
  .ctas { margin-top: 34px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 14px; align-items: center; }
  .fine { margin-top: 22px; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--ink-3); }

  .instrument {
    padding: 26px 28px 20px; border-radius: 14px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1c1e22, #121316);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.06), 0 0 0 1px #2a2d32, 0 30px 60px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6);
  }
  .inst-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .on-duty { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; color: var(--plasma-hi); }
  .lamp-on { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--plasma); box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--plasma); flex: none; }
  .instrument :global(.clock) { justify-content: center; }
  .inst-scale { display: flex; justify-content: space-around; margin-top: 12px; }
  .readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 20px; border-top: 1px solid #2a2d32; }
  .readout div { padding: 12px 6px 2px 14px; border-left: 1px solid #2a2d32; }
  .readout div:first-child { border-left: 0; padding-left: 4px; }
  .readout dd { font: 500 1.0625rem/1.2 var(--cond); letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--plasma); margin-top: 4px; }

  /* Section heads */
  .sec-head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr); gap: 24px 64px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 44px; }
  .sec-head .prose-m { padding-bottom: 6px; }

  /* Rack */
  .rack-sec { padding-block: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); background: linear-gradient(180deg, #111215, transparent 40%); }
  .rack {
    position: relative; padding: 10px 40px; border-radius: 10px;
    background: #101113;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule), 0 24px 60px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4);
  }
  .rack::before, .rack::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; top: 14px; bottom: 14px; width: 12px;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, #050506 2.5px, #2a2d32 3px, transparent 3.5px) 0 0 / 12px 44px repeat-y;
  }
  .rack::before { left: 14px; }
  .rack::after { right: 14px; }
  .ch {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 240px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px 48px; align-items: center;
    padding: 34px 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .ch:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .ch-feature { grid-template-columns: 240px minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); padding-block: 44px; }
  .ch-flip .ch-shot { order: -1; }
  .ch-flip { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) 240px minmax(0, 0.9fr); }
  .ch-read { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 12px; }
  .ch-read-pair { grid-auto-flow: column; justify-content: start; gap: 22px; }
  .ch-read-pair > div { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .plate { font-size: 0.75rem; color: #8a9098; }
  .ch-copy { display: grid; gap: 12px; justify-items: start; }
  .ch-copy .prose-m { max-width: 56ch; }
  .more {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin-top: 4px;
    font: 500 0.875rem/1 var(--cond); letter-spacing: 0.2em;     text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; padding-block: 8px;
  }
      .more:hover { color: var(--plasma-hi); }
  .more::after { content: ''; width: 30px; height: 1px; background: currentColor; transform: scaleX(0.6); transform-origin: left; transition: transform 0.2s var(--ease-out); }
  .more:hover::after { transform: scaleX(1); }

  .lamps { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .lamps li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7px auto; column-gap: 12px; align-items: center; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .lamps li .engr { grid-column: 2; font-size: 0.6875rem; }
  .lamp-step { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: #5a6068; flex: none; }
  .keyswitch { width: 120px; height: 64px; }

  /* Job run */
  .run-sec { padding-block: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); }
  .run { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: start; }
  .job-card {
    margin: 0; padding: 26px 28px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.05), 0 0 0 1px var(--rule-2);
    display: grid; gap: 12px;
  }
  .job-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-2); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .job-head .engr { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .job-card blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 10px; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 8px; background: #0f1012;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6), 0 0 0 1px var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.9875rem; line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .perm { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .perm li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .sw { flex: none; width: 30px; height: 16px; border-radius: 8px; background: #26292e; box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.7); position: relative; }
  .sw::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 2px; left: 2px; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: #5a6068; }
  .perm .on { color: var(--ink); }
  .perm .on .sw { background: #3a2410; }
  .perm .on .sw::after { left: 16px; background: var(--plasma); box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--plasma); }

  .trace { list-style: none; padding: 6px 0 0; display: grid; }
  .trace li { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px 1fr; column-gap: 18px; padding-bottom: 30px; }
  .trace li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 18px; bottom: -4px; width: 1px; background: var(--mesh); }
  .trace li.last { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .trace li.last::before { display: none; }
  .node { grid-row: span 2; width: 25px; height: 25px; border-radius: 50%; background: #121316; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--mesh); position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .node::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: #5a6068; }
  .trace .h3 { font-size: 1.375rem; padding-top: 1px; }
  .trace p { color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: 6px; max-width: 52ch; }

  /* Keys */
  .keys-sec { padding-block: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); background: linear-gradient(180deg, #121316, transparent); }
